WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.135
Let's make A little autumn leaf loom.

2
00:00:02.515 --> 00:00:07.300
Tie a small twig frame, stretch five strands across it and weave flexible leaves

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.325
through the spaces.

4
00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:10.785
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:13.895
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:14.275 --> 00:00:16.520
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.960
An adult checks twigs, helps tie corners and trims loose string.

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.095
Keep the frame flat while weaving and do not hang string outdoors.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.690
Step 1.

10
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.315
Lay out a square.

11
00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:34.503
Place four twigs in a square on the tray, overlapping each corner by about

12
00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:35.190
2 centimetres.

13
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.535
Choose leaves that bend gently without snapping.

14
00:00:38.915 --> 00:00:40.295
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:42.460
Check the twigs and leaves.

16
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.180
Step 2.

17
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.055
Tie the corners.

18
00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:51.700
At each crossing, wrap a short string three times around both twigs.

19
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.320
Cross the ends on the back and tie a firm double knot.

20
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.840
Repeat at all four corners while the frame stays flat.

21
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.600
Grown-up help.

22
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.065
Finish and check each corner knot.

23
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.845
Step 3.

24
00:01:06.225 --> 00:01:08.065
Add five weaving strands.

25
00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:13.188
Tie five strings from the top twig to the bottom twig, spaced about 2

26
00:01:13.188 --> 00:01:13.865
centimetres apart.

27
00:01:14.245 --> 00:01:17.445
Keep them snug but not so tight that the frame bends.

28
00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:19.810
An adult trims long tails.

29
00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.570
Grown-up help.

30
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.505
Tie or check knots and trim loose ends.

31
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.150
Step 4.

32
00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:28.970
Weave a leaf row.

33
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:34.749
Slide a leaf across the frame over the first string, under the second, and

34
00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:35.520
continue alternating.

35
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:40.000
Start the next leaf under the first string, then over the second.

36
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.575
Use gentle pressure; replace brittle leaves.

37
00:01:43.955 --> 00:01:45.335
Grown-up help.

38
00:01:45.715 --> 00:01:48.120
Help guide a leaf if it catches.

39
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.675
Step 5.

40
00:01:51.055 --> 00:01:52.410
Fill and admire.

41
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.080
Add leaves until the centre has a loose striped pattern.

42
00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.675
Stop before it becomes crowded.

43
00:01:59.055 --> 00:02:03.330
Keep the frame flat, give the artwork a title and gather all spare string.

44
00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.090
Grown-up help.

45
00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.240
Check loose strings and move the frame carefully.

46
00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:12.582
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

47
00:02:12.962 --> 00:02:16.512
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

48
00:02:16.892 --> 00:02:18.912
Your creation can look different.

49
00:02:19.292 --> 00:02:21.282
Remove and reuse the string.

50
00:02:21.662 --> 00:02:25.132
Sort twigs and leaves separately from other materials.

51
00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:28.857
Lay flat indoors to dry; leaves may fade or curl.

52
00:02:29.237 --> 00:02:30.227
Well done.

53
00:02:30.607 --> 00:02:33.037
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

